 "fitted_on_what_it_is_scored_on": "The rule that recognises a hashed stereo bond -- how short a mark is, how many make a ladder, how unequal their lengths must be -- was arrived at by running this on these ten drawings and reading the failures, so the score below is an upper bound on what the same code does on a drawing it has not seen. One constant was not fitted: the distance a bond stops from a label's text was measured over the hundred labels these cells carry, where the nearest endpoint is never more than 1.01 points away. A held-out check is available and not yet run: the metabolite rows state a pathway, so a rebuilt metabolite can be required to differ from its parent by the formula that pathway implies.",
 "reading": "A parent rebuilt exactly says the geometry of that drawing was read right. A parent rebuilt wrongly is a reading error of a kind the metabolite rows will make too, and the drug it happened on says which drawing feature caused it. The ten parents are the whole key the document offers; Sotorasib is scored by the summary without a table here, so there is no eleventh."
}